{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-a46cbdb2ab4af9b23a59","statement":"For quasi-compact ind-placid stacks, we do not have a direct analogue of <<ref:eq: identifying star sheaf with shrek sheaf-2>>. Namely, the category $\\cshv(X)$ and $\\scshv(X)$ (as defined in <<ref:shv over sshv>>) are very different in general, even with a choice of a generalized constant sheaf $\\La_X^\\eta$ (which we recall is in fact an object in $\\scshv(X)$ as explained in <<ref:rem: generalized constant sheaf on ind-placid stacks>>). However, we still have the tensor product\n\n\\begin{equation}\n\\fgshv(X)\\otimes \\fgshv(X)\\to \\fgshv(X),\\quad (\\mF,\\mG)\\mapsto (\\verd_X^\\eta)^{\\fg}(((\\verd_X^\\eta)^{\\fg}(\\mF))\\os ((\\verd_X^\\eta)^{\\fg}(\\mG))),\n\\end{equation}\n\nas <<ref:eq: eta tensor product on cshv>>. Note that this tensor product may not have a unit, but we still have\n\n\\begin{equation}\n\\Hom_{\\rshv(X,\\La)}(\\mF,\\mG) \\simeq \\Hom_{\\rshv(X,\\La)}((\\mF)\\otimes^\\eta (\\verd^{\\eta}_X)^{\\fg}(\\mG),\\consdual^{\\ind\\fg}_X), \\quad \\mF,\\mG\\in \\fgshv(X,\\La),\n\\end{equation}\n\nwhere $\\consdual^{\\ind\\fg}_X$ is as in <<ref:ex: indfgdualizing sheaf>>.\n\nWe will still use $\\otimes^\\eta$ to denote the ind-extension of <<ref:eq: eta tensor product on fgshv>>, which now becomes a (non-unital) monoidal product of $\\rshv(X,\\La)$.","source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"dcfba6a1c645263f278b336cb45ee2bce8fa272328e9b8979d4370fd741180f8","kind":"remark","label":"Remark 2","ref_key":"rem: equiv between cons-sheaf and cons-cosheaf-2","name":"","order":1190,"deps":[{"ref":"eq: eta tensor product on cshv","card_id":"ma-c-b9740731d260cb398abb","label":"Equation  eta tensor product on cshv","resolved":true,"target":"card"},{"ref":"eq: eta tensor product on fgshv","card_id":"ma-c-58f9f62a3acd70461385","label":"Equation  eta tensor product on fgshv","resolved":true,"target":"card"},{"ref":"eq: identifying star sheaf with shrek sheaf-2","card_id":"ma-c-f29bb3e7aed87ecaf21d","label":"Equation 2","resolved":true,"target":"card"},{"ref":"ex: indfgdualizing sheaf","card_id":"ma-c-63628dbb64754881df7f","label":"Example 852","resolved":true,"target":"card"},{"ref":"rem: generalized constant sheaf on ind-placid stacks","card_id":"ma-c-65c410306f6d6bd3ea62","label":"Remark 855","resolved":true,"target":"card"},{"ref":"shv over sshv","card_id":"ma-c-dee3c511d859d93bf9d9","label":"Remark 778","resolved":true,"target":"card"}],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.07482","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"1b700e8c4a2fc6f0c0f522039f223820ba6737a9a0ac91aea37c58ba7a3389c2","line":21579,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-28T11:10:54+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":1213,"math_hints":91}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","title":"Tame categorical local Langlands correspondence","abstract":"In one of our previous articles, we outlined the formulation of a version of the categorical arithmetic local Langlands conjecture. The aims of this article are threefold. First, we provide a detailed account of one component of this conjecture: the local Langlands category. Second, we aim to prove this conjecture in the tame case for quasi-split unramified reductive groups. Finally, we will explore the first applications of such categorical equivalence.","authors":["Xinwen Zhu"],"year":"2025","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.07482","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"fraka":"{\\mathfrak a}","frakb":"{\\mathfrak b}","frakc":"{\\mathfrak c}","frakg":"{\\mathfrak g}","frakh":"{\\mathfrak h}","frakm":"{\\mathfrak m}","frakp":"{\\mathfrak p}","fraks":"{\\mathfrak s}","frakt":"{\\mathfrak t}","fraku":"{\\mathfrak u}","frakA":"{\\mathfrak A}","frakC":"{\\mathfrak C}","frakM":"{\\mathfrak M}","frakX":"{\\mathf